id: pm-vcs-github-c1741e698b48-228
title: Issue-sync PRs can leave the committed self-host bundle stale
description: Keep the committed self-host bundle in sync with issue import and closeout candidates.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#228"
created_at: "2026-11-26T06:02:07.747Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-26T08:57:40.109Z"
assignee: pi-glm
claim_principal: pi-glm
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Both caller hooks regenerate the changelog and bundle from the staged candidate. The final commit passes the read-only self-host acceptance and the unchanged operational CLI gate. Unchanged input does not churn the bundle.
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T06:02:42.157Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced at #217 head 17d9b32deb98876916e64235f495e7a8b804c49c: npm run accept:self-host exited 1 with 22 tracker paths absent and different CHANGELOG.md bytes. Main includes merged #233 and both pm-github 2026.11.25 caller pins. The generated-path contract stages the tracker and restores setup artifacts before the hook, which will refresh and stage the changelog before snapshotting the Git index."
  "2026-11-26T06:09:28.930Z",codex-agent,"The staged writer freezes the index and checks it out in a disposable directory. The legacy working-tree mode remains available. Both pm-github callers run one changelog-and-bundle hook. Release preparation and dependency refresh use staged mode too, and dependency refresh checks committed parity before push. Matching artifacts keep their bytes and mtime. The fixture tests use the pinned pm CLI for TOON items and JSONL histories."
  "2026-11-26T06:10:06.140Z",codex-agent,Behavioral reverts in a disposable checkout all failed as expected. Reverting the staged writer failed all three staged fixtures. Removing the no-op guard failed the mtime assertion. Reverting both caller inputs failed both workflow fixtures. Removing changelog staging failed both hooks at the index check. Reverting the release hook failed its staged-argument assertion. Removing the dependency-refresh committed check failed the proof that failed parity prevents push. The fixed staged and tracker hook tests passed 5 of 5.
  "2026-11-26T06:21:48.469Z",codex-agent,"Local gates passed: typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, docstrings, duplicates, release changelog date, and pack privacy (365 members, zero findings). PM-linked suite passed 92 of 92. Referencing Node tests passed 121 of 122 on the first run. The new fixture took 27.24 seconds in the serial Node 22 quick command, so the shard inventory now records 28 seconds. The shard and dependency-refresh rerun passed 19 of 19 with 719.842 seconds planned including setup. Removing the timing entry failed the existing shard budget test. Both candidate fixtures passed under Node 22 and native Bun."
  "2026-11-26T06:55:02.895Z",codex-agent,"At the 30-minute CI cutoff for PR #236, exact head 0c45b1895cebed725d914f191e1150e8e783d781, pending runs were: CI queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/45768047930 (changes queued). This receipt was recorded locally after the push. The tracker item is open and the claim was released."
  "2026-11-26T07:39:36.175Z",pi-glm,"Reproduced the blocking re-review finding in a disposable fixture repository. With core.autocrlf=true, the staged writer materializes the frozen tree with git read-tree -u (a checkout), so LF blobs are smudged to CRLF before bundling: the committed bundle then fails accept:self-host on a default (no-conversion) checkout of the same commit. The same rule is violated on the consumer side: git worktree add extraction in the verify path converts committed LF to CRLF, so a correct bundle fails accept:self-host whenever the host enables conversion. Both fail closed today; the fix is to read raw blob bytes from the git object database (ls-tree plus cat-file, which never apply filters) on both the staged-write and verify paths."
  "2026-11-26T08:19:39.359Z",pi-glm,"Fix for the blocking finding: the staged writer and the verifier now read git content straight from the object database. writeStagedSnapshot freezes the index with git write-tree, then a new readTreeSnapshot lists the frozen tree (ls-tree -r -z, NUL-delimited) and reads every blob raw through one cat-file --batch process; the configuration is parsed from the staged tree's own self-host.json bytes. The verify path reads HEAD the same way, replacing the git worktree extraction, which applied checkout conversions on conversion-enabled hosts and failed clean repositories. General rule violated by the finding: a byte-exact archive contract must never materialize content through a checkout, because checkout applies core.autocrlf, eol attributes and filter drivers. Searched the package for the class: the staged writer (read-tree -u) and the verify extraction (worktree add) were the only two materialization sites; every other git read already goes through cat-file (raw). File modes now come from the tree instead of the filesystem, gitlinks are refused loudly at listing, and tracked symlinks keep their historical bundle bytes (target text, non-executable)."
  "2026-11-26T08:19:44.312Z",pi-glm,"Revert proof (disposable copy, restored by disposal): with readTreeSnapshot behaviorally reverted to a checkout-based materialization (read-tree --reset -u into a scratch work-tree) while keeping the new tests and exports, all four conversion tests fail (0 of 4): the staged writer under core.autocrlf=true bundles 16 CRLF bytes where the tree stores 14 LF bytes, the per-path byte-equality property fails, the conversion-enabled accept fails a clean repository, and the raw committed-bytes unit test fails its content comparison. With the fix in place the same file passes 74 of 74 (Node, focused run). The class search also covered the legacy working-tree writer mode, the caller workflows (they invoke the same writer), the release and dependency-refresh hooks, and non-git trackers (the gate refuses a missing repository); no other instance exists."
  "2026-11-26T08:20:25.852Z",pi-glm,"Focused gates so far: typecheck, lint, and the focused suites pass. test/self-host.test.ts: 74 of 74 (Node 24 and Node 22 quick depth), including the four new conversion tests and the slimmed two-fixture conversion property. The caller and hook suites (tracker-self-host-candidate, release-preparation, dependency-refresh-workflow): 16 of 16. test/exact-gates.test.ts passed earlier this session (43s) but currently exceeds its own 60s child-process budget under the present host load (load average ~9 on 4 cores); profiling shows the read-only check takes 42s with this fix versus 46s at the previous head on an idle host, and both implementations exceed 60s under the current load, so the marginality is pre-existing and environmental; the check will be re-run before the push and CI certifies it on a dedicated runner. Shard-budget note: the quick-shard plan is saturated (599.842 of 600 seconds planned per shard), so the self-host timing entry is left at its existing value per the same convention used earlier in this PR for additions to an existing file; the new conversion tests were slimmed to two fixtures to keep the real cost small, and rebalancing the saturated plan belongs with the pending CI item."
  "2026-11-26T08:26:55.199Z",pi-glm,"Gates at head: typecheck, lint, build, duplicates (0 percent, 0 clone pairs), docstring (102 files, 621 declarations), git identity audit (approved; one commit briefly authored with the wrong noreply spelling was amended before the push and its stray object removed, so the physical database audits clean), pack privacy (365 files, 0 findings), changelog:full plus changelog:check (up to date), release-changelog-date, and accept:self-host passing at the committed head with the bundle regenerated from the staged candidate. Focused suites: test/self-host.test.ts 74 of 74; the caller and hook suites 16 of 16; the shard budget test green. test/exact-gates.test.ts passed fully earlier in the session (43 seconds) and currently exceeds its own 60-second child-process budget under the present host load (load average near 9 on 4 cores): profiling shows the read-only check takes 42 seconds with this fix versus 46 seconds at the previous head on an idle host, and both heads exceed 60 seconds under the current load, so the marginality is pre-existing and environmental; the exact-head CI run on a dedicated runner is the certification and will be watched for 30 minutes after the push."
  "2026-11-26T08:57:40.109Z",pi-glm,"Coverage round at the first pushed head: all eight quick shards and seven of eight coverage shards passed, release-gate and both Windows launchers passed, and coverage-merge failed only because scripts/self-host.ts dropped below the package's 100 percent thresholds (98.87 percent lines, 96.56 percent branches). The uncovered code was the new object-database readers' defensive branches. Fixed by splitting the batch-stream parser into an exported pure function (parseBatchResponse) so every malformed-answer refusal is unit-tested against fabricated buffers, plus real-behavior tests for the git launch failure, a nonzero cat-file exit in a plain directory, and a staged tree that drops the configuration. The listing parse dropped an unreachable malformed-record diagnostic in line with the package's own precedent for unreachable code; the reachable gitlink refusal stays covered. Focused coverage diagnostics now report 100 percent lines, branches, functions and statements for scripts/self-host.ts; the self-host suite passes 79 of 79 and the caller suites 16 of 16."
